# Whether an interval of the round-up interval is the empty set: its upper bound is a NaN (the empty
# set is (NaN, NaN), and no lane of a nonempty state is one); the default interval_empty_1 on the
# meaning. Exact, in every rounding mode (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Predicates and
# comparisons"). Requires the rounding mode upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and the options of
# docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_empty_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
output:        mask m
requires:      upward xu xn
ensures:       certain m empty x x=xu,xn exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the upper bound tested for a NaN (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeUpwardPredicates.v upward_empty_1_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand
unused:        xn the upper bound alone tells the empty set (NaN, NaN) from a nonempty state, whose lanes are no NaN

m = unord(xu, xu)
